# Requirements: Biweekly Structure Report Notifier

**Version:** 0.1 · **Date:** 2026-10-29 · **Owner:** Daniel · **Business owner:** [TBD: Who signs off for the report owner?]

## 1. Problem
Every two weeks the report owner sends one email by hand to every assignee and reporter on the structure report. The work is manual. The report owner researches odd cases by hand.

## 2. Current process
| Step | Who | Tool | Time per cycle |
|---|---|---|---|
| The page updates itself from Jira queries that Eric set up | Automatic | Confluence, Jira | None |
| Send one email with the US and NULSC page links | Report owner | Email | [TBD: How many hours does one send take?] |
| Research an unassigned or inactive person (rare) | Report owner | Jira ticket | [TBD: How long does one case take?] |

**Total today:** [TBD: hours per month]

## 3. Users
The assignees and reporters get the email every two weeks. Eric's team uses the output. Daniel runs it by hand from a Nelnet laptop. Daniel maintains it first, then Eric's team including Dave.

## 4. Success metric
A dry run gives the same findings and recipients as the report owner's next round. [TBD: What number shows it works, and how many hours does it save?]

## 5. Scope
**In (v1):**
- Read the queries from the US page at run time.
- Apply the page rules. An epic needs a milestone as its parent, and the exclusion label takes it off the report.
- An in-progress initiative needs a start date of today or earlier and an end date of today or later. Neither date can be blank.
- A milestone needs an initiative as its parent. The fix deadline is two weeks.
- Send one email per run date to every assignee and reporter with a finding. Remove duplicates. The body has the page link only.
- Put a recipient that cannot be resolved on an exception list. Send the list to the Odd Squad mailbox.

**Out (v1):**
- Publishing the page, unless Dave asks.
- A CAB approval rule, a team lead list, and one message per lead.
- Teams delivery, hosting, a runner, and an unattended service account.
- NULSC, until step N1 passes and Eric or the security owner authorizes it in writing.

## 6. Inputs and outputs
| Input | Source | Access status |
|---|---|---|
| Page queries | US Confluence Data Center page | Requested |
| Issues, assignees, reporters | US Jira, through the page queries | Requested |
| Parent link field | Jira | Blocked [TBD: Which Jira field holds the parent link?] |
| Sender address | Odd Squad mailbox | Requested (RITM1089333) [TBD: Which address does the email send from?] |

**Output:** one email over SMTP, one exception list email, and a local sent record. Read-only runs only, until Eric says otherwise.

## 7. Where AI is used
| Step | What the model does | Human review point |
|---|---|---|
| None | The slice makes no model call | The report owner compares the dry run with her round before the first send |

## 8. Risks
| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| The process stops after a send and before the record | A recipient can get two emails | The maintenance guide shows how to reconcile. [TBD: Does Eric approve this limit?] |
| The page query and our rules give different findings | The comparison run shows a difference | [TBD: Is a finding what the page query returns, or what our rules decide?] |
| Delegated send takes about 2 weeks | The first real send is late | File the request early. It is not filed yet |

## 9. Acceptance criteria
- [ ] A dry run matches the report owner's next round and sends nothing.
- [ ] A run date gets one email with no duplicate recipients and the page link only.
- [ ] A run with no findings sends no email.
- [ ] An unresolved recipient goes on the exception list. The list is not guessed.
- [ ] A failed send writes no record. A retry for a recorded run date sends nothing.
- [ ] Slice 2 writes nothing to Jira.
- [ ] Eric's team uses the output. [TBD: What evidence of use does Eric want?]

## 10. Open questions
- [TBD: What is the check for a story? The email has four sections and the rules cover three.]
- [TBD: Is the exclusion label p/o_not_applicable or p/c_not_applicable?]
- [TBD: Does the email use To or Bcc?]
- [TBD: Does a US-only first release meet the acceptance bar?]
- [TBD: What is the not-available value for the first linked child?]
